<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net9.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational" Version="9.0.14" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Agents.AI.OpenAI" Version="1.0.0-rc2" />
    <!--
      MUST move in lockstep with Microsoft.Extensions.AI.Abstractions.

      The `Anthropic` package below forces Abstractions from 10.3.0 up to 10.5.1, and 10.5.1
      RENAMED seven public types that Microsoft.Extensions.AI 10.3.0 still references:
      FunctionApproval{Request,Response}Content, McpServerToolApproval{Request,Response}Content,
      UserInput{Request,Response}Content and IToolReductionStrategy became
      ToolApproval{Request,Response}Content / Input{Request,Response}Content.

      Those references sit in FunctionInvokingChatClient (ExtractAndRemoveApprovalRequestsAndResponses,
      TryReplaceFunctionCallsWithApprovalRequests, ...) — the client that `IChatClient.AsAIAgent()`
      puts on EVERY agent's request path, for every provider. Left at 10.3.0 against Abstractions
      10.5.1, the first agent run throws TypeLoadException on Azure OpenAI and vLLM too, not just
      Anthropic — and `dotnet build`/`dotnet test` both pass, so nothing catches it before runtime.

      Deliberately NOT bumping Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI to 10.5.1 alongside: it requires
      OpenAI >= 2.10.0, which would NU1605 against the pinned OpenAI 2.8.0 (Azure.AI.OpenAI tops out
      at 2.9.0-beta.1). Its own dangling references are confined to the Responses-API conversion
      helpers (ToOpenAIResponseItems, ToChatMessages, FromOpenAIStreamingResponseUpdatesAsync), and
      this solution uses Chat Completions via ChatClient.AsIChatClient(), so they are never JITted.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.AI" Version="10.5.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="Azure.AI.OpenAI" Version="2.8.0-beta.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenAI" Version="2.8.0" />
    <!--
      Official Anthropic .NET SDK (the `Anthropic` package is first-party from v10 onward; 3.x and
      below were the community tryAGI build, now `tryAGI.Anthropic`).

      Transitive dependencies it declares for net9.0, all of which unify UPWARDS across the
      solution — verify with `dotnet list package` with the include-transitive flag after changing this:
        - Microsoft.Extensions.AI.Abstractions 10.5.1  (NOT a benign minor bump over the 10.3.0
          that Microsoft.Agents.AI.OpenAI pulls in — it renamed seven public types, which is why
          Microsoft.Extensions.AI is pinned to 10.5.1 above; see that comment)
        - System.Net.ServerSentEvents 10.0.1           (already present transitively at 10.0.3)
        - System.Text.Json 10.0.6                      (WIDEST BLAST RADIUS: a 10.x assembly in a
          net9.0 app, affecting every JsonSerializer call in the engine — the video-analysis
          artifacts, ExtractStepConfig, every structured-output schema — not just Anthropic calls)
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Anthropic" Version="12.49.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.Abstractions" Version="9.0.14" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Binder" Version="9.0.9" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
